Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
an exclusive Copyright upon the creator of an original work. In some
jurisdictions, this copyright protection is extended automatically to
derivative works. In most jurisdictions, copyright protection is
generally for the life of the author plus a fixed number of years.

In some jurisdictions, it is possible to voluntarily relinquish all
copyright rights in a work, thereby placing it in the public domain.
CC0 is a universal form of relinquishing all copyright rights, and
is accepted by all jurisdictions that have signed the Berne Convention.

The person who associated a work with this deed has dedicated the work
to the public domain by waiving all of his or her rights to the work
under copyright law, including all related and neighboring rights, to
the extent allowed by law. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform
the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission.

To the extent possible under law, the person who associated a work with
this deed has waived all copyright and related or neighboring rights
to this work.